*  stackover.sno -- recurse until the interpreter stack runs out.
*  ERRORS: DOWN calls itself and never returns. Error 21, at sixty-six
*  levels. STSIZE is 1000 descriptors, which the historical source
*  chose at line 253 of engines/sil-v3.11.sil, and how many levels
*  that buys depends on the frame: this function takes one argument
*  and gets sixty-six, while A(3,0) in ackermann.sno takes two and
*  runs out at forty-two.
*  Part of github.com/mdhender/sil. BSD 2-Clause; see LICENSE.
*
*  It is the failure -stack exists to move. Run it by hand with a
*  bigger one and it goes further before it stops:
*
*      sil -stack 35k stackover.sno
*
*  and ackermann3.sno is the program that does that on purpose.
-LIST
        DEFINE('DOWN(N)')                        :(DOWN.END)
DOWN    DOWN = DOWN(N + 1)                       :(RETURN)
DOWN.END
        OUTPUT = 'going down'
        OUTPUT = DOWN(1)
END
